          "body": "I know you're copying from what's done elsewhere in the dissector so this isn't really your fault, but this (and elsewhere) doesn't actually work and will cause a dissector bug error to be added to the tree.\n\n`proto_tree_add_string` cannot be called on a field whose field type is not a string. `DISSECTOR_ASSERT_FIELD_TYPE_IS_STRING(hfinfo)` is called inside `proto_tree_add_string`.\nEither `proto_tree_add_int64_format_value` (mutatis mutandis whatever field type) where some default value (e.g., 0 for ints) has to be used along with the string value for format (and add the expert info), or else some other special error hf.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-03-02T14:35:46.351Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-03-02T14:35:46.351Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 459990669,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 23735,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0f4786a0f6ffc8d2f9d80166717cb16f96b75f12",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3124937654,
          "type": null,
          "body": "that's a very good point and I was also a bit confused if my changes would work actually. After further reviewing the dissector and the additional resources files comments, it is more clear.\n\nProbably something like this?:\n```\nti = proto_tree_add_uint64_format_value(subtree, child_field->hf_value, tvb,\ntoken->start, token_len, 0, \"Cannot convert value: %s\", child->value);\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
